# Where the Warzone weapon catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-09-23**. `catalog.json` in this folder is the
list; this file says where every fact and every picture in it came from.

**Pictures: publisher artwork only (decision D116).** Every picture in
`weapons/` is Activision's own image, downloaded from callofduty.com or its
image server imgs.callofduty.com, converted to PNG, cropped to the weapon and
scaled to at most 480 x 300 pixels. None came from a fan wiki, Fandom, a loadout
site or an image search. They are Activision's copyright, used in the app to
identify the weapon, the same risk the owner accepted for the game pictures in
D116. Delete a `.png` and set that weapon's `image` to `null` and the app shows
the class symbol instead; nothing else changes.

## What is in Warzone today

- **Current season: Season 06, "The Haunting"**, live since September 17, 2026
  ([Season 06 blog](https://www.callofduty.com/blog/2026/09/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-warzone-season-6-the-haunting-announcement), [Warzone Season 06 patch notes](https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes/2026/09/call-of-duty-bo7-warzone-season-06-patch-notes)).
- **Integrated premium title: Call of Duty: Black Ops 7.** Its weapons came to
  Warzone with Season 01 on December 4, 2025 ([Season 01 blog](https://www.callofduty.com/blog/2025/11/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-warzone-zombies-season-01),
  [Warzone Season 01 patch notes](https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes/2025/12/call-of-duty-bo7-warzone-season-01-patch-notes)). They fill the normal class tabs.
- **Legacy weapons: Modern Warfare II, Modern Warfare III and Black Ops 6.** The
  Warzone Season 01 patch notes say weapons from these three "remain accessible
  and usable in Call of Duty: Warzone", reached by scrolling to the far right of
  the class tabs to the Legacy menu; the same notes then say "Legacy Weapons
  moved to a new Legacy tab in the Weapons menu". They get none of the Black Ops 7 extras
  (Prestige, BO7 camos, build codes). Later notes still fix Legacy-weapon bugs
  ([Season 01 Reloaded](https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes/2026/01/call-of-duty-bo7-warzone-season-01-reloaded-patch-notes), [Season 03 Reloaded](https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes/2026/04/call-of-duty-bo7-warzone-season-03-reloaded-patch-notes): "Legacy Weapons would
  remain disabled in standard playlists after exiting a Ranked Private Match
  lobby", so Ranked turns them off; [Season 05 Reloaded](https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes/2026/08/call-of-duty-bo7-warzone-season-05-reloaded-patch-notes)), so they are
  still in the game in the season this list was made.
- **Not yet in Warzone: Modern Warfare 4.** It launches October 23, 2026 and
  Warzone takes its content from its Season 1 ([announcement](https://www.callofduty.com/blog/2026/05/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-announcement)). The
  Modern Warfare 4 beta weapons that some loadout sites already list are not
  in Warzone.

Counts: 270 weapons in 21 groups. Black Ops 7: 64. Legacy: 206 (Black Ops 6 69,
Modern Warfare III 60, Modern Warfare II 77).

