## Rarity (`tiers`, read 2026-09-23, D134)

- **The five rarities and their colours are Activision's words:** the [Black
  Ops Royale deep dive](https://www.callofduty.com/blog/2026/03/black-ops-7-black-ops-royale-battle-royale-deep-dive)
  lists "five main, color-coded rarity values", Common (Grey) to Legendary
  (Orange), with one to five attachments, and gives Exotic Weapons "the Ultra
  (gold) rarity level".
  Battle Royale's notes use the same words ("awarded at grey rarity", "moved to
  purple rarity", [Season 02 patch notes](https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes/2026/02/call-of-duty-bo7-warzone-season-02-patch-notes)).
- **Loadout** is the colour of the player's own loadout guns: the [Black Ops 6
  Season 01 patch notes](https://www.callofduty.com/patchnotes/2024/11/call-of-duty-bo6-warzone-season-01-patch-notes)
  moved infil and respawn weapons off "a single custom loadout color" and onto
  a rarity colour, so the loadout colour is now the loadout gun's alone.
  Its red was read off 2025 and 2026 gameplay video frames, not an official
  image: rough.
- **Ultra** is Black Ops Royale's only (Exotic Weapons, usually eight
  attachments); Battle Royale and Resurgence have Common to Legendary plus
  Loadout.
- **The colours** in `tiers` were sampled from Activision's compressed WebP
  images and are good to about 10 a channel. They are the app's display
  colours; the Core learns its own from the owner's crops.
- **Where the HUD shows it:** the name stays white; right after it, a small
  icon in the tier's colour (a chevron and a diamond with 0 to 4 pips; a bar
  and a cross on a loadout gun); a line under the ammo count; in Black Ops
  Royale also brackets round the build name ([Activision's HUD screenshot](https://imgs.callofduty.com/content/dam/atvi/callofduty/cod-touchui/blog/body/bo7/black/BO7-SO2R-BLACK-OPS-ROYALE-026.webp)).
  The gun's HUD picture has cyan attachments on every gun, whatever its tier.
- **Not confirmed:** exact attachment counts per tier outside Black Ops
  Royale; the loadout icon's exact shape; whether Common's icon is grey or
  white; every hex value. Community pages (the Fandom "Rarity" template,
  TheGamer 2020, Gfinity 2023) agree on the five colours and disagree on
  Common's white or grey.
- **Refresh:** each season's Warzone patch notes; a new tier goes at the end of
  `tiers`, never renumbering the others.

## How the list is organised, and what is not confirmed

- **Black Ops 7 classes, in the game's order.** Activision's own [Black Ops 7
  weapons guide](https://www.callofduty.com/guides/blackops7/weapons) filters by Assault Rifle, SMG, Shotgun, LMG, Marksman Rifle,
  Sniper Rifle, Pistol, Launcher, Special, Melee, the same order the Warzone
  Season 01 patch notes list them in. The names are written in the plural, as
  the [launch blog](https://www.callofduty.com/blog/2025/11/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-ready-for-launch-weapons-equipment) and the patch notes write them, and "Special" as they do.
- **Order inside a class**: the launch weapons in the order the Warzone Season
  01 notes list them (the free weapon first, then by the player level that
  unlocks it), then each later weapon in the order its season added it. **The
  order on the in-game screen itself was not confirmed** from an official page.
- **Legacy groups.** The game keeps every Legacy weapon behind one Legacy tab.
  Community guides ([timesaver.gg](https://timesaver.gg/blog/warzone-bo7-unlock-level-legacy-weapons),
  read 2026-09-23) say it is split by class and then by game; Activision says
  nothing about its inside. So the catalog has one group per class,
  "Legacy Assault Rifles" and so on, and **those group names are ours, not
  labels read off the screen**. Inside a group: Black Ops 6, then Modern
  Warfare III, then Modern Warfare II; for Black Ops 6 and Modern Warfare III
  launch weapons in their launch blog's order then seasonal ones in release
  order; for Modern Warfare II roughly launch then seasonal (no official page
  lists its launch weapons by name). The Modern Warfare titles' "Battle Rifles"
  stay their own group (Black Ops 6 Warzone kept them as a class); their
  "Handguns" are in Legacy Pistols; the Riot Shield is in Legacy Melee, where the
  Modern Warfare III launch blog counts it.

