## Uncertain

- `pistols.coda_9` (Coda 9): Capitalisation only: Activision writes 'Coda 9' (launch blog, patch-note text) and 'CODA 9' (weapons guide, Season 01 notes) about equally; the game sets names in capitals, so both read the same on screen.
- `special.nx_ravager` (NX Ravager): Class: the Warzone Season 01 patch notes list it under Special, but Activision's Black Ops 7 weapons guide page labels it Sniper Rifle (its own picture there is named SPC). Filed under Special until the owner's screen says otherwise.
- `melee.flatline_mk_ii` (Flatline Mk.II): Capitalisation only: the launch blog writes 'Flatline Mk.II', several patch notes 'Flatline MK.II'; the game sets names in capitals.
- `legacy_launchers.torque_35` (Torque 35): Class: both official Modern Warfare III pages call this compound bow a Launcher; one community loadout site files it as a Marksman Rifle. Kept as a Launcher.
- `legacy_melee.riot_shield` (Riot Shield): Availability: covered only by Activision's general statement that Modern Warfare II weapons remain usable in Warzone; no Black Ops 6 or Black Ops 7 era Warzone patch note names the Riot Shield, so its place in today's Legacy menu is unconfirmed.

## Community sites, used only to cross-check

Nothing in the catalog was taken from these; they were read to catch a missed
weapon or to learn what Activision does not say.

- [wzstats.gg](https://wzstats.gg/), its embedded weapon list, read 2026-09-23.
  Its Black Ops 7 list matches ours (64) except that it lacks the Season 06
  Arcblade and files the Special weapons under Launcher; for the Legacy titles
  it lists only weapons people build loadouts for (no Modern Warfare II melee or
  launchers), splits conversion kits out as separate weapons, and already lists
  Modern Warfare 4 beta weapons, which are not in Warzone. Every weapon it lists
  that is in Warzone is in the catalog.
- [timesaver.gg, "How to Unlock & Level Legacy Weapons in Warzone"](https://timesaver.gg/blog/warzone-bo7-unlock-level-legacy-weapons)
  and [Game Rant, "How to Access Armory Unlocks & Legacy Weapons"](https://gamerant.com/cod-black-ops-7-bo7-warzone-wz-armory-unlocks-legacy-content-how-to-get/):
  the Legacy tab sits at the far right of the weapon classes (both), split by
  class and then game (timesaver.gg only).

